; Four links, none of which reaches a file this model can read, and one which
; does not exist at all in a directory holding no observation file whatsoever.
;
; They are four different mistakes and are reported as four: a file which is
; not there is not the same finding as a path which leaves the model, and
; telling somebody "the observations are wrong" when what is wrong is an
; extension is how a five-second fix becomes an afternoon.
(node site:S-101
  (label "Meeting Room A")
  (kind Space)
  (type MeetingRoom)
  (geometry area)
  (frame frame:site)
  (observed-in "observations/2026-05-07-interior.obs"))

(vertex geom:V-01
  (label "Room A, north-west corner")
  (frame frame:site)
  (observed-in "../elsewhere/2026-05-06-site-control.obs")
  (observed-in "observations/2026-05-06-site-control.dfc"))

(vertex geom:V-02
  (label "Room A, north-east corner")
  (frame frame:site)
  (observed-in "observations/2026-05-07-interior.obs"))

; The two ways a path stops meaning one thing on every machine. Both are
; refused wherever the model is read rather than wherever they happen to be
; dangerous: a link one clone follows out of the model root and another refuses
; is worse than either behaviour on its own.
(vertex geom:V-03
  (label "Room A, south-east corner")
  (frame frame:site)
  (observed-in "observations\\2026-05-06-site-control.obs")
  (observed-in "C:/surveys/2026-05-06-site-control.obs"))
